1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:06,387
In customer discovery, I heard: Finding a bond’s CUSIP is such a pain.

2
00:00:06,387 --> 00:00:12,374
I don’t know where to buy. Fidelity’s bond account is not for me.

3
00:00:12,374 --> 00:00:16,058
I only want to invest a small amount.

4
00:00:16,058 --> 00:00:19,282
Different comments, one design challenge: getting started.

5
00:00:25,400 --> 00:00:30,288
How can someone with no bond experience understand a few options and make

6
00:00:30,288 --> 00:00:33,672
their first small purchase? That’s the question behind InCreditble.

7
00:00:37,400 --> 00:00:41,155
First, I tell the product I’m new to bonds.

8
00:00:41,155 --> 00:00:44,076
That changes how much explanation I get.

9
00:00:44,076 --> 00:00:49,501
My risk preference is separate. Then I choose a yield target, a timeframe,

10
00:00:49,501 --> 00:00:54,090
an industry and a budget. Let’s start with just twenty-five dollars.

11
00:00:59,400 --> 00:01:03,406
I don’t need to start with a bond identifier.

12
00:01:03,406 --> 00:01:07,412
The finder gives me three matches within my preferences.

13
00:01:07,412 --> 00:01:13,198
I can compare an earlier repayment date, a different industry and more interest,

14
00:01:13,198 --> 00:01:15,424
with the important trade-offs visible.

15
00:01:20,400 --> 00:01:25,346
When I need help, I can ask about the company or what could

16
00:01:25,346 --> 00:01:30,293
go wrong. Here, the assistant explains the risk of missed payments and selling

17
00:01:30,293 --> 00:01:34,098
early. The explanations are optional; the decision stays with me.

18
00:01:39,400 --> 00:01:45,035
Now I see a sample price, with separate buy and sell quotes.

19
00:01:45,035 --> 00:01:48,792
My twenty-five dollars buys part of a bond.

20
00:01:48,792 --> 00:01:54,897
Before confirming, I can see exactly what I pay, the cash I’ll have

21
00:01:54,897 --> 00:01:58,184
left, expected interest and the repayment date.

22
00:01:58,184 --> 00:02:01,471
These are promised payments, not guaranteed returns.

23
00:02:07,400 --> 00:02:12,041
After I approve, the new holding appears and my cash balance updates.

24
00:02:12,041 --> 00:02:15,909
The payment view helps me see when interest is expected.

25
00:02:15,909 --> 00:02:20,936
Existing sample accounts stay visible alongside this position, so I can see the

26
00:02:20,936 --> 00:02:21,710
wider picture.

27
00:02:25,400 --> 00:02:31,613
Underneath, explicit filters and transparent ranking narrow a pool of 672 fictional bonds.

28
00:02:31,613 --> 00:02:36,870
The prototype tracks fractional positions, settlement, cost basis and payment schedules.

29
00:02:36,870 --> 00:02:41,171
Assistant responses, identity checks, quotes and connections are simulated;

30
00:02:41,171 --> 00:02:44,994
no live AI model or broker is connected.

31
00:02:46,400 --> 00:02:51,981
Next, we’ll test whether first-time investors can explain their purchase and its risks

32
00:02:51,981 --> 00:02:55,844
without coaching. InCreditble. Your first bond. At your pace.
